note over Core,Trust #violet: 0. Load ETDA Trusted List (when a transaction needs it)
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] steps in the ETDA Trusted List Load sequence (first tab)

note over User,CoreApp #lightblue: 1.1 User Login
User->CoreApp: Login (PIN / biometric)
CoreApp->CoreApp: Login with Tang Rat to get Token
CoreApp-->User: Login completed , show Tang Rat home

note over CoreApp,DW #lightblue: 1.2 Request VC Issuance
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] a credential is added to the wallet only when its data comes from the source of truth (section 2) and it is issued and verified by the wallet (sections 8 , 9)\nany issuance problem returns an error
User->Mini: Choose a credential type to request
Mini->CoreApp: Check holder key exists on this device
CoreApp->CoreApp: Check holder key exists on this device\n(key alias in Android Keystore / Secure Enclave)
CoreApp-->Mini: Holder key found / not found
alt Holder key not found on device (first use of Document Wallet on this device)
    Mini->CoreApp: Create and register the holder key
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• 13.4 (MUST NOT)  server component of the wallet
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW Core is a fully trusted part of the wallet , the app calls only DW Core , attestations and proofs are made on the device
    CoreApp->DW: Register the wallet unit and get a challenge (nonce for the platform attestation and the holder key binding) + Token | POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/challenge (DW endpoint 01)\n(deviceId , provider , role = WALLET , os)
    note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] the same user registers a new wallet unit on the same device (app removed and installed again , the old keys are gone from the keystore)\nwhether DW revokes the old wallet unit at once (client_status = 1 , cascade in Revoke-Suspend-Reactivate CASE C) is decided by the DW team\nanother device of the same user is a separate wallet unit and is not revoked
    DW->DW: Register the wallet unit (wallet unit id , os) and create the challenge (nonce for the platform attestation and the holder key)
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store the holder key challenge in DW database
    CoreApp<--DW: wallet unit id , challengeId , challenge , expiresAt
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Create the attestation key with the challenge and get the platform attestation\nAndroid Key Attestation (StrongBox) / iOS App Attest
    note right of CoreApp #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.2 (MUST)  holder key in a WSCD\n• chapter 14 SC-20 (informative)  WSCD attestation before issuance
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Generate holder key pair with the DW challenge as attestation challenge (Secure Enclave / Android Keystore / StrongBox)\nAndroid : Key Attestation certificate chain of the holder key | iOS : App Attest assertion over the holder public key and the challenge
    CoreApp->CoreApp: Sign the DW challenge with the holder private key\nSign the wallet attestation request proof with the instance key
    CoreApp->DW: Activate wallet unit , get the wallet attestation and register the holder key + Token | POST /dw/v1/holder-keys/register (DW endpoint 02)\n(attestation , attestation key proof , device signing key proof , wallet attestation proof , signedChallenge , challengeId , publicKey ,\nholder key attestation : Android certificate chain / iOS App Attest assertion)
    DW->DW: Check app integrity\nAndroid : Google attestation CA , package name , signing certificate , security level | iOS : Apple App Attest root CA , bundleId
    note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 12.2 (MUST) : mapping of StrongBox , TEE , Secure Enclave to key_storage not published | accepted types and iOS evidence : wallet team
    DW->DW: Verify the platform evidence of the holder key and signedChallenge with publicKey\nAndroid : certificate chain to the Google root , attestationChallenge = challenge , key in StrongBox or TEE | iOS : App Attest assertion over the holder public key and the challenge
    alt App integrity or holder key evidence failed
        DW->DW: Set wallet unit status = ERROR , [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = DEVICE_ATTESTATION_FAILED)
        CoreApp<--DW: Error
        CoreApp-->Mini: Wallet cannot be activated on this device
        Mini-->User: Show error , a credential cannot be added on this device
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , sections 1.3 to 11 do not apply
    else Evidence valid
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] EUDI TS3 v1.5.2\n• 2.5.1  large status list , random index\nToken Status List draft-21\n• 12.1 , 12.2  herd privacy\nThai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 10.5.2  WIA and KA status lists
        note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] DW guidance : at least 10000 entries per list , published at DW endpoint 16
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Allocate a random unused idx for this wallet unit in a WIA status list of at least 10000 entries , no per-user uri\nkey_storage_status entry = the shared entry of the key storage type (Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 section 10.5.2 item ก)
        note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID4VCI 1.0\n• Appendix E  Wallet Attestation (WIA)
        DW->DW: Sign the wallet attestation (WIA) with the wallet provider key of DW\ncnf = instance key , client_status = { uri of DW endpoint 16 , idx }\nheader x5c = wallet provider certificate (no iss) | cnf , wallet_name , wallet_version , wallet_solution_certification_information , wallet_link , client_status { status , exp }
    end
    DW->DW: Verify signed challenge with publicKey\n[DATA STORE] Store holder public key , key storage type , WIA idx , key_storage_status entry , wallet unit status = ACTIVE , device status = HOLDER_BOUND
    CoreApp<--DW: Wallet unit activated , WIA , holder key registered
    CoreApp->CoreApp: [DATA STORE] Store WIA of this wallet instance
    CoreApp-->Mini: Holder key registered
else Holder key found
    Mini->Mini: Continue
end
Mini->DW:Request a credential + Token (from Tang Rat login) | POST /dw/v1/issuance/requests\n(DW endpoint 03) (CitizenId , deviceId registered with the holder key ,\ncredential type = OrgCode , Source , ServiceCode)\n+ IdP ID token
Mini-->User: Show processing (wait for response of 1.2)
DW->DW: Validate Token and CitizenId (CitizenId = Token owner)\n(also checked against pid of the IdP ID token in 1.3)
note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (issuance request)\nissuanceSessionId (created by DW)\nCitizenId (from the request , checked with the Token)\ndeviceId\nrequested credential type (OrgCode , Source , ServiceCode)\nstatus\nrequestedAt
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store issuance request in DW database
DW->DW: Look up holder key of this device in DW database\n(look up by deviceId , device status = HOLDER_BOUND)

alt Holder key of this device not registered
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED\n(credential not issued)
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_NOT_ACTIVATED\nnextAction = REGISTER_HOLDER_KEY
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , the app registers the holder key (section 1.2) and the user requests the credential again
else Holder key registered
    DW->DW: Continue to 1.3
end

note over DW #lightblue: 1.3 Validate ID Token

alt IdP ID token provided
    DW->DW: Load the signing keys of the IdP that issued the ID token (cached)
    note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] OpenID Connect Core 1.0\n• 3.1.3.7  ID Token Validation
    DW->DW: Verify ID token\nsignature (IdP JWKS , ES256) , iss = IdP , aud = client_id registered with the IdP , exp , nonce
    DW->DW: Check pid in ID token = CitizenId of the request

    alt ID token invalid / pid mismatch
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID)
        Mini<--DW: Reject issuance request\nreason = IDENTITY_ASSURANCE_INVALID
        Mini-->User: Cannot proceed , please log in again
    else ID token valid
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database (identity assurance profile)\nial stored as IAL level\niss stored as KYC source\nauth_time stored as last authentication timestamp\namr stored as last authentication method (if provided)\npid stored as citizenId\nissued ID token reference (jti) stored in audit
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store identity assurance profile in DW database
    end
else No IdP ID token (existing session)
    DW->DW: Use identity assurance profile stored at last login
end

note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] identity assurance profile : identityAssuranceId , citizenId , IAL , AAL , KYC source , KYC timestamp , assurance expiry , last authentication method and time
DW->DW: Load existing identity assurance profile

note over DW,Engine #violet: 1.4 Get Schema Details
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] two callers : DW Core (this flow) and agency systems (system to system) | steps marked caller channel = WALLET run only for DW Core
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] VCVPAuditLog for every request , also those rejected at the Consumer-Key check (OrgCode and Actor empty) , kept 7 years
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 8.6 , 8.8 (MUST)  audit log at least 7 years
DW->Core: Get the default schema of the requested credential type | POST /api/credential-schema/v1/default (VCVP Core 07)\nOrgCode , Source , ServiceCode
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) and its permission for this endpoint\ncaller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN
alt Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
    DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 1.4.1 to 11 do not apply
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Continue to Read Schema
end
note over DW,Engine #orange: 1.4.1 Read Schema
Core->Core: Look up the credential type of OrgCode + Source + ServiceCode (CredentialTypes , Status = ACTIVE)\nthen its default schema (CredentialSchemas.CredentialTypeId , IsDefault = true)
alt Credential type or default schema not found
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] the credential type and schema are created by the issuing agency , not during issuance
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = CREDENTIAL_TYPE_NOT_FOUND or SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND , EngineCalls)
    DW<--Core: 404 | FailureReason = CREDENTIAL_TYPE_NOT_FOUND or SCHEMA_NOT_FOUND
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = FailureReason\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = FailureReason
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 1.4.2 to 11 do not apply
else Schema found
    Core->Core: Map CredentialSchemaId to ENGINE_CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID and the engine to call\n(ENGINE_CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID = CredentialSchemas.EngineRefs[].RefCredentialSchemaId , engine = EngineRefs[].EngineName)
    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] one central WALLET Consumer-Key , issued by VCVP administrators to DW Core only | the agency opts in per schema , checked again in section 5
    Core->Core: Check permission by caller channel\nWALLET (DW central Consumer-Key) : the agency allows requests from the wallet on this schema (CredentialSchemas.AllowWalletRequest)\nother channels : the schema belongs to the caller's organisation

    alt Wallet request not allowed by the agency
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 (FailureReason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED , EngineCalls)
        DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED\n(credential not issued)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 1.4.2 to 11 do not apply
    else Wallet request allowed
        Core->Core: Continue to read schema details
    end
end


note over DW,Engine #orange: 1.4.2 Read Schema Details
Core->Engine: Get schema details | GET /api/credential-schema/v2/{ENGINE_CREDENTIAL_SCHEMA_ID}
Core<--Engine: 200 | schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | Name | Type | Required)
Core->Core: [AUDIT LOG] Write audit record of VCVP Core 07 : who read which schema (EngineCalls)
DW<--Core: 200 | CredentialSchemaId , RequiredLoA (of the credential type , CredentialTypes) , schema details + Claims[] (ClaimId | Path | NameEn | NameLocal | Type | Required)

note over DW #lightblue: 1.5 Check Identity Assurance Level
DW->DW: Take RequiredLoA of the credential type (section 1.4)
DW->DW: Validate assurance\nstill valid (assurance expiry) , meets required freshness ,\nIAL level ≥ RequiredLoA

alt Assurance invalid / expired / not fresh / IAL below RequiredLoA
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = STEP_UP_REQUIRED\n(VC not issued , this request ends here)
    Mini<--DW: Response of 1.2 : request step-up verification or re-KYC | reason , RequiredLoA
    Mini-->User: Show message : identity verification is not enough for this credential type (reason , RequiredLoA)\nask the user to verify identity again in Tang Rat before continuing
    Mini->DW: Submit verification result (new IdP ID token) | POST /dw/v1/identity-assurance/step-up (DW endpoint 04)
    DW->DW: Verify new ID token (same checks as above)
    DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store updated identity assurance profile in DW database
    DW->DW: Validate assurance again

    alt Still not sufficient
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = LOA_INSUFFICIENT)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of step-up) | reason = LOA_INSUFFICIENT
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    else Assurance sufficient
        Mini<--DW: 200 (response of step-up)
        Mini->Mini: Send request 1.2 again for the same credential type\n(the new request runs from section 1.2 with the updated identity assurance)
    end
    note over User,Mini #wheat: This request stops here , sections 2 to 11 do not apply to it

else Assurance valid
    DW->DW: Continue to Read Data
end

note over DW,Agency #lightgray: 2. Read Official Data
note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] user session : citizenId
DW->DW: Look up applicant data in DW database

alt No data in DW database
    DW->Agency:Fetch applicant data from agency

    alt Data not found / not authorized
        DW<--Agency: Not found | Not authorized
        DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = AGENCY_DATA_NOT_FOUND / AGENCY_NOT_AUTHORIZED)
        Mini<--DW: Return reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
        Mini-->User: Show reason (Not found 404 | Not authorized 403)
    else Agency data available
        DW<--Agency: Applicant data + SyncDate
        note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nsourceFetchedAt = SyncDate\nsourceLastUpdatedAt = from agency if available\nsourceSystem = Government API Source of Truth\ncachePolicy = reuse data in DW database if it already exists\ncacheKey = citizenId + documentType\ncacheInvalidation = on revoke / suspend / expire
        DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store applicant data + SyncDate in DW database
    end

else Data already exists
    DW->DW: Use applicant data from DW database
end

DW->DW: Validate official data & Check status active & Check not suspended &\nCheck not revoked etc.

alt Official data invalid
    DW->DW: Update status SOURCE_DATA_INVALID
    DW->DW: [ERROR AUDIT] Store DW audit log (FailureReason = SOURCE_DATA_INVALID)
    Mini<--DW: Reject issuance request
    Mini-->User: credential not eligible
else Official data valid
    DW->DW: Continue to Prepare Data
end


note over DW #lightgreen: 4. Prepare Data
note right of DW #wheat:[SPEC] check SyncDate against MaxDataAgeDays before requesting issuance , older data is fetched again (section 2)
DW->DW: Map data to Claims[] based on schema details from VCVP Core 07\nSet OrgCode of the issuing agency\n(IssuerIdentityId and IssuerKeyId are not sent , VCVP Core selects them in section 5.1)

note right of DW #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] DW evidence of the claims prepared for this request , proves what data DW sent for issuance\nauditHash = hash(canonical audit payload)\nauditSignature = sign(auditHash) (optional)\npreviousAuditHash = link to previous log\nretentionPolicy = at least 7 years (Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 sections 8.6 and 8.8)\nretentionUntil = issuedAt + retention period\nimmutableStorage = WORM / append-only log
note right of DW #wheat:[STANDARD] ISO/IEC 27002:2022\n• 8.15  logging\nISO/IEC 27701:2025\n• A.3.25  PII logging\nMDES notice on computer traffic data B.E. 2564\n• clauses 9 , 12  integrity , keep at least 90 days
note right of DW #FFCDD2:[PENDING] ISO wording taken from secondary summaries , confirm against the purchased ISO/IEC 27002:2022 and 27701:2025
DW->DW: Create tamper-evident audit record of the mapped claims (DW audit log)

note right of DW #wheat:[DATA STORE] DW database\nissuance request\nmapped claims\naudit log\nidentity assurance reference
DW->DW: [DATA STORE] Store mapped claims + audit log in DW database (issuance request)

note over DW,Core #lightgreen: 5. Request Issuance and Validate Request
DW->Core: Request credential issuance | POST /api/credential/v1 (VCVP Core 08)
Core->Core: Check Consumer-Key (DW Core central Consumer-Key) and caller authorization\ncaller channel = WALLET , ActorType = CITIZEN\nthe schema belongs to the agency of OrgCode (CredentialSchemas.OrganizationId)\nWALLET : CredentialSchemas.AllowWalletRequest = true | other channels : OrgCode is the organisation of the caller's Consumer-Key
alt Caller not authorized
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08\n(FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED / WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED , OrgCode and Actor empty when the Consumer-Key is invalid)
    DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = CALLER_NOT_AUTHORIZED / WALLET_REQUEST_NOT_ALLOWED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = FailureReason\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = FailureReason
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
else Caller authorized
    Core->Core: Continue
end

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] CredentialSchemaId is still the default of its credential type (IsDefault) , else 409 SCHEMA_NOT_DEFAULT\nIssuerIdentityId and IssuerKeyId are optional : identity of the schema owner and ACTIVE , key of that identity (Keys.IdentityId) and ACTIVE\na key with Keys.Status = REVOKED (compromised) : FailureReason = ISSUER_KEY_COMPROMISED (Key-Compromise-sequence)
Core->Core: Validate the request against the schema\n(default schema , claims , issuer identity and key when sent)
alt Schema is no longer the default of its credential type
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_DEFAULT)
    DW<--Core: 409 | FailureReason = SCHEMA_NOT_DEFAULT
    DW->DW: Get the default schema again (section 1.4) and repeat sections 4 and 5
else Claims or issuer identity / key invalid
    note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] VCVPAuditLog\nFailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED\nMessageCode , Message (HTTP status of the error)\nEventTime\nActor (OrgCode , ConsumerKey , Channel)\nCorrelation.RequestId
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED / ISSUER_KEY_COMPROMISED)
    DW<--Core: 400 | FailureReason = REQUEST_REJECTED / ISSUER_KEY_COMPROMISED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = FailureReason\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = FailureReason
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
else Request valid
    Core->Core: Continue
end

Core->Core: Validate SyncDate against CredentialSchemas.MaxDataAgeDays
alt Source data older than MaxDataAgeDays
    note right of Core #wheat:[ERROR AUDIT] VCVPAuditLog\nFailureReason = SOURCE_DATA_TOO_OLD\nMessageCode , Message (HTTP status of the error)\nEventTime\nActor (OrgCode , ConsumerKey , Channel)\nCorrelation.RequestId
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = SOURCE_DATA_TOO_OLD)
    DW<--Core: 400 | FailureReason = SOURCE_DATA_TOO_OLD
    DW->Agency: Fetch applicant data from agency again
    DW->DW: Repeat sections 2 to 5 with the new data and SyncDate
else Source data within MaxDataAgeDays
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end

note over Core,Engine #orange: 5.1 Check Issuer Setup

note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] organisation , issuer key and DID are prepared by the agency in setup , missing one = no VC
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.7  DNSSEC for .go.th

Core->Core: Look up agency organisation in Organizations table (OrgCode)
Core->Core: Use the issuer DID of the schema (CredentialSchemas.IssuerIdentityId)\nuse IssuerIdentityId instead if the caller sent it\nengine to call = CredentialSchemas.EngineRefs[].EngineName
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] key status RESERVED / ACTIVE / DEPRECATED / REVOKED , one ACTIVE key per identity , more than one = configuration error\nVCVP Core always sends issuer and issuerKey to the engine
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 13.7.7.1 (informative)  key lifecycle states
Core->Core: Use the ACTIVE key of that DID , set by the agency in setup (Keys.Status = ACTIVE , Keys.IdentityId)\nuse IssuerKeyId instead if the caller sent it\nsent to the engine as issuerKey , stored in Credentials.IssuerKeyId (section 6)

alt Organisation / issuer DID not found , or more than one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08\n(FailureReason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_DID_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_KEY_AMBIGUOUS)
    DW<--Core: Reject issuance request\nFailureReason = ORGANISATION_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_DID_NOT_FOUND / ISSUER_KEY_AMBIGUOUS
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_SETUP_NOT_FOUND
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 5.1.1 to 11 do not apply
else Organisation and issuer DID found , at most one ACTIVE key
    Core->Core: Continue
end

note over Core,Trust #violet: 5.1.1 Check Trust Framework
note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 9.8 (MUST)  Trusted List checks\n• 12.7 (informative , MUST)  not found = failure
note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] this check at issuance is a VCVP policy , the wallet checks the issuer again (part 2 sections 7.1 , 9)
note right of Core #FFCDD2:[PENDING] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0 page 12.1 , 12.1.4 , 12.1.5 : the Issuer Trusted List has no published field for the credential types an issuer may issue\n(credential_types is a proposal only) and no field for the credential_issuer URL , the credential type check waits for the Thai profile\nthe engine vct changes with each schema version (/ssi/vct/v2/{orgId}/{schemaId}/SD_JWT_VC)
Core->Core: Look up the issuer in the cached Issuer Trusted List (iss.txt , ETDA Trusted List Load)\nissuer DID and signing key listed (ServiceDigitalIdentity) , organisation and service status = active , validity period current ,\ncredential type (vct) within the issuer scope
note right of Core #wheat:[AUDIT LOG] proof that the issuer passed the Trusted List check at issuance (VCVPAuditLog.TrustCheck)\ntrust validation result stored in TrustCheck.Result\ntimestamp stored in TrustCheck.CheckedAt\nTrusted List reference (LoTESequenceNumber , entity id) stored in TrustCheck.RegistryReference\nWritten once with the audit record of this request , never updated
Core->Core: Keep trust validation result (for the audit record of VCVP Core 08)
Core->Core: Validate the issuer passed every Trusted List check
alt Trust validation failed
    Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = TRUST_FAILED , TrustCheck)
    DW<--Core: 403 | FailureReason = TRUST_FAILED
    DW->DW: Update issuance request status = TRUST_FAILED\n(credential not issued)
    Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = TRUST_FAILED
    Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
    note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 5.2 to 11 do not apply
else Trust validation passed
    Core->Core: Continue issuance
end


note over Core,Engine #orange: 5.2 Issuer Key Check

Core->Core: Check the issuer key from section 5.1 (Keys.Status , Keys.ExpiryDate)

alt No ACTIVE key / key expired (Keys.ExpiryDate passed)

    alt Next key reserved in the issuer DID is available
        note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] the reserved key is already in the DID (added when the DID was created , VCVP Core 03)\nthe switch changes only Keys.Status , no engine call , the next issuance sends the new key as issuerKey
        Core->Core: Switch issuerKey to the next reserved key in the DID\n(Keys.Status RESERVED → ACTIVE)
    else No reserved key left in the DID
        note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] no key is created during issuance , the agency creates a key (VCVP Core 02) and adds it to the DID (VCVP Core 40) in setup
        note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 12.6 (MUST)  Trusted List update within 24 hours after a rotation
        Core->Core: [ERROR AUDIT] Write audit record of VCVP Core 08 (FailureReason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED)

        DW<--Core: Reject issuance request\nFailureReason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        DW->DW: Update issuance request status = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED\n(credential not issued)
        Mini<--DW: Error (response of 1.2) | reason = ISSUER_KEY_EXPIRED
        Mini-->User: Show error , credential not added (reason)
        note over User,Mini #wheat: Issuance stops here , credential not added , sections 6 to 11 do not apply
    end

    note right of Core #wheat:[SPEC] old key = DEPRECATED , kept for verification , new key for new credentials | compromised key : Key-Compromise-sequence (VCVP Core 36)
    note right of Core #wheat:[STANDARD] Thai VC ARF 2.0 DRAFT 0\n• 13.7.7.1 (informative)  old key stays in assertionMethod
